<div class='readmoretextdiv indrevlineclamp' data-lines='3' data-revid='565'>				We brought Luna to Safari on a Sunday because she had been sick for three weeks and diagnosed / treated for rhinitis, but was still having symptoms and clearly not feeling well.  Dr Garner immediately identified that she had a cracked premolar, which was likely abscessed.  The tooth was extracted that day, the infection cleaned out, and Luna was put on medications for two weeks.  After only 2 days, Luna was back to herself, kissing us and rolling over for a belly rub :)</div>
